{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CfgcrnJWdXgh2vbDY9i1M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is structurally clean and idiomatic:\n\n- **Logic stays in the right unit.** The holiday rule lives entirely inside `BusinessDays`, the existing single home for the business-day roll. No logic leaks into callers or a new catch-all.\n- **Good decomposition.** Extracting `isBusinessDay(LocalDate)` removes the weekday/weekend/holiday predicate from `rollToBusinessDay`, so the roll loop reads declaratively and the predicate is expressed once rather than duplicated.\n- **The loop generalizes cleanly.** Replacing the hard-coded Saturday/Sunday `+2`/`+1` branches with a `while (!isBusinessDay)` roll-forward is the natural way to handle consecutive non-business days (e.g. a holiday adjacent to a weekend) without special-casing, and it preserves the idempotence property documented in the Javadoc.\n- **Constant placement and naming fit.** `HOLIDAYS` as a `private static final Set.of(...)` is the conventional way to hold a fixed lookup set, and `Set.contains` is the idiomatic membership check.\n- **Docs kept in sync.** Both the class and method Javadoc were updated to describe the new behavior, matching the repository's documentation style.\n\nNo duplication, no misplaced responsibility, nothing becoming a catch-all — a maintainer of this codebase would find this natural."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7062,"cache_read_input_tokens":11894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7062},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02ddb68f-af91-40e4-be98-e1bdc4171d47","uuid":"479ae6bc-3f66-458b-b4c5-8952cfd1f96e